{"resourceIdentifier":"5022","resourceName":"Reduction of Enteric Methane Emissions using Feed Additives on Dairy Farms in the Netherlands","description":"FrieslandCampina is the largest dairy company in the Netherlands and one of the top five dairy companies in the world. Structured as a cooperative, it is owned by its 15,137 member farms across the Netherlands, Belgium and Germany. In an effort to reduce greenhouse gas (GHG) emissions from the livestock sector, FC has introduced feed supplements into the daily feed of dairy cows on member farms in the Netherlands. The additives aim to reduce emissions from enteric fermentation in the rumen of dairy cows. The project has a 10-year fixed term and will run to 2032, and over the course of the project lifetime, FrieslandCampina aims to introduce new feed additives across its farms in the Netherlands. The project estimates average annual reductions of approximately 750,000 tCO2e.","location":{"latitude":52.132600,"longitude":5.291300},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2024-06-20","endExclusive":"2024-07-21","endInclusive":"2024-07-20"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"5022"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Multiple Provinces"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"FrieslandCampina C.V."},{"type":"string","value":"Utrecht, Netherlands"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Registered"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"631036"}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Livestock, enteric fermentation, and manure management"}]},{"code":"PROTOCOL_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"VM0041"}]},{"code":"VALIDATOR_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Earthood Services Limited"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_REGISTRATION_DATE","value